```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `AdminPassword` | string | yes | Password for the web UI login. Without one, anyone with the URL can use the UI, so always set it. The OSC entrypoint hashes it (PBKDF2-SHA256) into the SALTED_PASS variable at startup and does not keep the plain value. Feeds ADMIN_PASSWORD, which exists only in our OSC fork (upstream reads SALTED_PASS). Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |
| `FetchWorkers` | string | no | Number of pages fetched in parallel (FETCH_WORKERS), a whole number. Defaults to 5 when empty; lower values use less memory. |
| `PageWatchLimit` | string | no | Maximum total number of watches allowed (PAGE_WATCH_LIMIT), enforced in the UI, imports and the API. Empty or non-numeric means unlimited. |
| `DisableVersionCheck` | boolean | no | Set to true to stop the app checking for new upstream releases (DISABLE_VERSION_CHECK). Off by default. |
| `Timezone` | string | no | Default timezone as an IANA name, for example Europe/Stockholm (TZ). Used for watch schedules and date/time expressions in notifications. Defaults to UTC. |
| `LoggerLevel` | string | no | Log verbosity (LOGGER_LEVEL), for example INFO or WARNING; case-insensitive. When empty the app logs at DEBUG, which is very verbose, so INFO is recommended. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
